  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">humanitarian assistance for war victims in Snihurivska community (Mykolaiv region)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the Snihurivska community of the Mykolaiv region was shelled by the Russian military. On Easter night on April 16, Russian Armed Forces attacked the city of Snihurivka: 2 schools were destroyed, a hospital and a cultural center were damaged, more than 30 residential buildings were damaged, and power lines were damaged. In the village of Vasylivka, about 30 private residential buildings were damaged and a school building caught fire. The required relevant assistance is related to the restoration of households after damage and destruction (building materials, boards and timber for the roof, roofing, windows, doors, other non-food products. To meet this category of needs, it is necessary to determine the needs of each household separately.</narrative>
  </description>
